{
    "article_summary": "The article describes a catalytic asymmetric radical aminoperfluoroalkylation and aminodifluoromethylation of alkenes using a dual Cu(I)/chiral phosphoric acid (CPA) catalytic system. By employing fluoroalkylsulfonyl chlorides as radical sources and silver carbonate as a chloride scavenger, the authors successfully synthesized enantioenriched alpha-tertiary pyrrolidines bearing various fluoroalkyl groups (C4F9, CF3, CF2CO2Me, CF2H) with high yields and excellent enantioselectivity.",
